# Build output. Never committed, always regenerated.
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# The generated WebAssembly loader (docs/06-limits.md §3). It is build output:
# not committed, not edited, regenerated on every build.
/crates/web/pkg
/crates/web/dist

# Credential path configuration (D-0013). The canonical location is outside the
# repository at ~/.brutex/credentials.toml; these entries exist so that a copy
# made inside the working tree for convenience still cannot be committed.
/credentials.toml
/.brutex-credentials.toml

# Criterion output.
/target/criterion

# cargo-mutants output. Build output, and it writes `.json` — which CI gate 1b
# confines to `.github/` and `crates/web/`.
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old
# Pre-external-drive mutation snapshots are preserved locally for recovery but
# remain generated evidence, not repository source. Root the pattern so a
# deliberately named fixture below a crate is not hidden.
/mutants.out*.pre-wd-black-*

# Editor and agent scratch. `.claude/` holds `launch.json` and
# `settings.local.json`, and `.json` is NOT in CLAUDE.md section 2's allowed
# extension list at all — CI gate 1b confines `.json` to `.github/` and
# `crates/web/`, so a single `git add -A` here would turn the build red. The
# directory is local tooling, not source; it is ignored rather than deleted so
# the tooling keeps working. See docs/05-decisions.md D-0028.
# THE OPERATOR TOOLING DIRECTORY, EXCEPT THE ONE FILE THAT IS THE PRODUCT.
#
# `.claude/` holds a local settings file and scratch worktrees, neither of
# which belongs to anyone but the machine they are on. `launch.json` is
# different: it is the Run configuration, and after D-0064 made the binary
# serve the front end it is the ONLY thing standing between a fresh clone and
# a working application. Ignored, it meant "clone and press Run" depended on
# IntelliJ inferring a Cargo target rather than on anything this repository
# promises — the IDE's guess, not the project's contract.
#
# Gate 1b already admits `.claude/` alongside `.github/` for exactly this
# reason: it is configuration, not source, and it is not shipped.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/launch.json

# Source maps: built by `vite build`, never tracked. Measured at 3.0 MB across
# 26 files against a 940 kB artifact, rewritten whole on every rebuild, in a
# tree that already commits `web/build` under D-0068. `vite.config.js` sets
# `sourcemap: 'hidden'` so nothing requests the files that are not here.
web/build/**/*.map
web/saved-backtest/build/**/*.map

# SCRATCH AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT, WHICH GATE 1 CANNOT SURVIVE.
#
# `a.txt` and `b.txt` have sat here since 2026-08-14 holding a 60-line copy of
# `normal_cdf` lifted out of `crates/greeks/src/normal.rs`. `.txt` is on NO
# allowlist — not CLAUDE.md section 2's, not gate 1's `allowed_names` — so a
# single `git add -A` stages them and gate 1 goes red on a file nobody meant to
# track. Nothing but nobody-typing-that-command was keeping the build green.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted, the same way `.claude/` is: a scratch copy of a
# function being edited is somebody's working state, and the hazard here is
# TRACKING it, not having it. Rooted with a leading slash so a `.txt` fixture
# under `crates/` or `web/` is still a deliberate decision rather than a silent
# omission.
/*.txt

# macOS.
.DS_Store

# The rolling log, written into the project root so the Run window and the
# project tree show the same thing. `crates/api::served_log_dir` picks this
# path when the process starts from a Cargo workspace, which is what pressing
# Run does. Untracked: gate 1 walks TRACKED files, and `.ndjson` is on no
# allowlist — a committed log would be the build failure CLAUDE.md section 2
# describes.
logs/
# `logs` is now a symlink to the external WD_BLACK tree; the slash-only rule
# above matches a directory but not that symlink. Historical migration
# snapshots are likewise retained locally and must never enter gate 1.
/logs
/logs.pre-wd-black-*

# IntelliJ. Untracked but NOT ignored until now: a single `git add -A` would
# stage `.idea/*.xml`, and `.xml` is on no gate 1 allowlist. The same hazard the
# `.claude/` block above is written for, for the other editor directory.
.idea/

# Local operator config and logs. These live in ~/.brutex, not here — but a
# stray copy inside a PUBLIC repository is the failure mode §8 exists to prevent,
# so the pattern is denied by name rather than by where the file happens to sit.
/.env
/server.log
**/.env
**/*.log
seq-run/
